# "If this spell was cast from a graveyard" asks where the spell was cast from (CR 601.2a), not whether flashback was used:
# cast from the graveyard by the escape Underworld Breach gives it ({1}{G} and three other cards exiled from the graveyard,
# CR 702.138a), Esper Origins still exiles itself and enters transformed as Summon: Esper Maduin with a finality counter.
# Turn 1: cast from hand (surveil bins Lightning Bolt and Island; 22 life); Black Lotus pays for the Breach and is
# sacrificed, so the graveyard holds Esper Origins, Lightning Bolt, Island and Black Lotus. The escape exiles the other
# three and the spell surveils (Forest and Llanowar Elves kept on top) and gains 2 (24). Chapter I then reveals the Forest
# and puts it into Bot1's hand. Exile holds the three escape cards and not Esper Origins, which is on the battlefield.

